{"kind":"request","text":"Document-only edit to notes/2026-10-15-self-contained-applications.md, section 5.1 \"The presentation trust model\": record that the MCP Apps extension is the owed boundary design.\n\nWhy: section 5.1 says the host owns reads, signing and custody, that package screens run in a separate origin that holds no keys, and that \"the design of the frame, the messages and the confirmations is still owed\". The MCP Apps extension (io.modelcontextprotocol/ui, stable 2026-01-26) is that design, and MVP S2 is building to it. Forge contract 4.7 says the same boundary in its own words.\n\nProposed text, to be added after the sentence \"The design of the frame, the messages and the confirmations is still owed.\":\n\n\"The MCP Apps extension of the Model Context Protocol (io.modelcontextprotocol/ui, stable 2026-01-26) is that design. A package's screens are ui:// resources. A host renders each one in a sandboxed frame on a separate registrable domain that holds no keys, and the frame talks to its host only by JSON-RPC over postMessage. Tool calls, model context and messages go through the host, which holds the member's keys and signs. The host's approval of a call that a screen started is the confirmation. The desktop AI apps used for the MVP test already implement the host side, and the reference host in the extension's repository shows the double-frame sandbox. dap's own page becomes one more host of the same screens, with \u003cid\u003e.inguz.space as the per-application sandbox origin, so that the browser, MCP and agents consume one presentation (section 3, principle 6; forge contract 4.7). MVP S2 builds the screens and the kit. The dap web host is a later request. Until it lands, M1's rule that the dap page installs only trusted packages still holds, while the chat hosts already provide the boundary.\"\n\nAlso in section 4's package table, change the Presentation row's Destination from \"Static assets in the package, bound to the projections\" to \"ui:// resources in the package, bound to the projections and served by the room's MCP endpoint\", and add a cross-reference to forge contract 4.7 beside section 5.1's heading.\n\nConditions: the edit lands as a document-only change under the testing guide's document-only gate handling, with no runtime, declaration or package change; checker review; the quoted text may be reworded for the note's voice but keeps each claim; the M1 request 74f38c24 is unchanged by this edit.","body":{"conditions":"Section 5.1 of notes/2026-10-15-self-contained-applications.md gains the paragraph quoted in the statement, reworded only for voice; the section 4 Presentation row and the forge 4.7 cross-reference are updated; the change is document-only under docs/testing.md handling; checker review; M1 request 74f38c24 unchanged.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}